+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** RC2.1 shipped the `reference_call` lifecycle table (with the `'skipped'` status already in the enum per amendment A6); RC2.2 shipped the `'viewed'` application status and the exact call site where the trigger must hook (`maybe_send_shortlist_notification`, `application_detail_handler.gleam:679`). Nothing yet CREATES `reference_call` rows. RC2.3 is the TRIGGER story: it connects the viewing to the reference schema — when a landlord marks the viewing done, the system auto-creates the `queued` reference-call rows for the right referee slots (the sweep, a later story, owns every actual send). It also lands the landlord's manual control surface: start a check pre-viewing, and skip/re-enable individual references before or at trigger.
+
+**Approach:** No schema migration (RC2.1 already added `'skipped'`; the briefing's migration step is stale — verified against `supabase/migrations/20260731222000_create_reference_call.sql:48`). A new `server/src/reference_checks/trigger.gleam` module owns one core creation function shared by the auto-trigger and the manual-start API; a post-commit hook at the `maybe_send_shortlist_notification` call site fires it on the transition INTO `viewed`; three authenticated landlord API arms (start / skip / re-enable) ride alongside the existing application routes; three new `AuditEvent` variants (`reference_call_created` / `reference_call_skipped` / `reference_call_re_enabled`) record the lifecycle. New Squirrel queries: an idempotent `INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` keyed on the live-slot partial unique index, a focused application reference-data read, and a dedicated re-enable (re-arms `next_attempt_at = now()`).
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- **No migration.** `'skipped'` is already in `reference_call_status` (RC2.1, A6) and `update_reference_call_status.sql` already clears `next_attempt_at` on entry to `'skipped'`. `audit_log.event_type` is `TEXT` (not a PG enum — verified `00000000000001_initial_schema.sql:164`), so new event wire-strings need no migration. The briefing's "Migration: ALTER TYPE ... ADD VALUE 'skipped'" step is STALE and is NOT performed.
+- **Hook position:** a new post-commit sibling call `maybe_trigger_reference_checks(config, app_uuid, landlord_uuid, vacancy_uuid, new_status)` placed IMMEDIATELY after `maybe_send_shortlist_notification(...)` in `apply_status_update`'s success branch (`application_detail_handler.gleam` ~line 685). Same posture as the shortlist notification: post-commit, fail-open (status already committed; a trigger failure is observability-only via Sentry, the response goes out regardless).
+- **Core creation function `reference_checks.trigger.create_checks`** is the single code path for BOTH the auto-trigger and the manual-start API (DRY; the AC mandates manual start creates "rows exactly as the auto-trigger would"). It: (1) reads the application's reference data + `never_rented_before` + `reference_contact_choice`; (2) SUPPRESSES entirely when `reference_contact_choice = 'declined'` (FR-RC3, A4 — the feature is off for that application); pre-v1 rows (NULL choice) and `'attested'` proceed; (3) selects the primary applicant's slots — `landlord_ref` (or `character_ref` when `never_rented_before` is true) PLUS `employer_ref`; (4) skips any slot whose contact trio has NO contact data (no name, or no reachable email AND no phone); (5) for each remaining slot runs the idempotent insert; (6) writes a `reference_call_created` audit row for each ACTUALLY inserted row; all inside one `pog.transaction` so the batch is atomic (both slots or neither).
+- **Idempotency (FR-RC3 double-trigger):** the insert is `INSERT ... ON CONFLICT (application_id, ref_slot, owner_label) WHERE status NOT IN (terminals) DO NOTHING RETURNING id::text`. The conflict target is the existing `idx_reference_call_live` partial unique index (predicate copied verbatim from `20260731222000_create_reference_call.sql:138`). A double-click, re-marking viewed, or manual-start-after-auto are all silent no-ops. A pre-existing `'skipped'` row ALSO conflicts (A6 — skipped occupies its slot), so a landlord-pre-excluded slot is respected by the trigger. `RETURNING` yields 0 rows on conflict (no audit), 1 row on insert (audit written).
+- **Slot selection rule (FR-RC3):** the landlord/character slot is ONE slot — `landlord_ref` when the applicant rented before, `character_ref` when `never_rented_before`. The employer slot is independent. So at most TWO rows are created per trigger. Owner label is always `'primary'` in v1 (co-applicant employer refs are schema-ready but deferred — AD-13).
+- **Skip API (FR-RC4 + A6):** idempotent, handles both "at trigger" and "before trigger" per A6. (a) If a `'skipped'` row already occupies the slot → no-op, 200. (b) If a `'queued'` row exists → guarded transition `queued → skipped` via the existing `update_reference_call_status` (which clears `next_attempt_at`). (c) If NO live row exists → create a `'skipped'` row directly with the contact snapshot (reserves the slot against a later auto-trigger's `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`). A `'skipped'` row always carries the contact snapshot from the application trio so a later re-enable has someone to chase. Audit `reference_call_skipped` on the effective transition/creation.
+- **Re-enable API (FR-RC4 + A6):** dedicated `re_enable_reference_call.sql` — guarded `UPDATE ... WHERE id = $1 AND status = 'skipped' SET status = 'queued', next_attempt_at = now() RETURNING id`. The existing `update_reference_call_status` cannot express this (its `next_attempt_at` CASE only clears or preserves, never re-arms to `now()`). 0-row → 404 (no skipped row to re-enable). Audit `reference_call_re_enabled`.
+- **Routes (FR-RC4 API, authenticated, CSRF via standard POST middleware, ownership via `ai_sql.verify_application_ownership` + archived-vacancy precheck — the `handle_update_status` pattern):**
+  - `POST /api/v1/vacancies/:vid/applications/:aid/reference-checks/start` — whole-application manual start (calls the core creation function; declined-suppression applies identically).
+  - `POST /api/v1/vacancies/:vid/applications/:aid/reference-checks/:slot/skip` — `:slot` ∈ {`landlord_ref`,`character_ref`,`employer_ref`} (validated via `shared.ref_slot_from_string`; unknown → 400).
+  - `POST /api/v1/vacancies/:vid/applications/:aid/reference-checks/:slot/re-enable`.
+- **Audit (AD-16):** three new `AuditEvent` variants — `ReferenceCallCreated` → `"reference_call_created"`, `ReferenceCallSkipped` → `"reference_call_skipped"`, `ReferenceCallReEnabled` → `"reference_call_re_enabled"`. `entity_type` is the free string `"reference_call"`. Within the trigger's own `pog.transaction`, the row-creation and its audit are atomic (Tier 1 inside the trigger tx — never create a row without its audit). At the OUTER level the whole trigger is fail-open post-commit (Tier 2 — the status is already committed). The synchronous API handlers (manual start / skip / re-enable) return errors to the client (not fail-open) because they are request-scoped, not background side-effects.
+- **No sends.** The trigger and manual-start create `queued` rows with `next_attempt_at = now()` and send NOTHING. The sweep (RC3.5) owns every send (AD-14). `insert_reference_call_if_absent` stamps `now()` via SQL, not Gleam.
+- **Copy:** no em-dashes in any user-facing copy (RT global ban, CI-guarded). Error strings are brand-voice ("Couldn't ...", never "Failed ...").
+- **Squirrel discipline (RC2.1 lessons):** nullable non-text columns read as `COALESCE(x::text, '')`; nullable TEXT contacts read `Option(String)`; nullable contacts written via `NULLIF($n, '')`; run Squirrel against the LOCAL Docker test DB directly (`cd server && DATABASE_URL=… gleam run -m squirrel`), NEVER via `run_squirrel.sh` (it sources `.env` and points at staging) and NEVER against staging/production. Revert any whitespace-only churn in `server/src/ai/sql.gleam` after each regen.
+
+**Ask First:** changing the slot-selection rule (e.g. also creating `character_ref` alongside `landlord_ref`); making the trigger in-transaction with the status UPDATE (would change the fail posture); a per-slot manual-start variant (the whole-application start + skip covers the UX).
+
+**Never:** no migration (RC2.1 already added `'skipped'`); no `DROP`/`RENAME` on any enum or column (expand-only); no sends / sweep / Twilio / form logic (RC3.x); no reference-detail payload extension (`reference_calls[]` on the detail GET is RC4.1); no landlord-facing UI / panel (RC4.x); no edits to `reference_call` / `reference_objection_log` / `consent_type` / `application_status` schema; no `let assert` in production code; no JS FFI; no em-dashes in copy; never commit env files or secrets.
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|---------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| Auto-trigger (rented before) | app → viewed, choice≠declined, landlord_ref has email, employer_ref has email | 2 rows created `queued` (`landlord_ref` + `employer_ref`), `next_attempt_at=now()`, 2 `reference_call_created` audits | N/A |
+| Auto-trigger (never rented) | app → viewed, `never_rented_before=true`, character_ref has phone | rows for `character_ref` + `employer_ref` (NOT `landlord_ref`) | N/A |
+| Skip no-contact slot | landlord_ref has no email AND no phone | NO row created for that slot; other slot(s) created normally | N/A (silent skip) |
+| Declined attestation | `reference_contact_choice='declined'` | NO rows created for any slot; no audits | N/A (suppressed) |
+| Pre-v1 application | `reference_contact_choice IS NULL` | rows created normally (AD-2 pre-v1 rule) | N/A |
+| Double trigger | viewed clicked twice (or manual-start after auto) | Second trigger is a no-op (`ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`); no duplicate rows, no duplicate audits | N/A |
+| Pre-excluded slot | landlord skipped `landlord_ref` BEFORE viewing, then viewed | auto-trigger's `landlord_ref` insert conflicts with the skipped row → no-op; `employer_ref` still created | N/A |
+| Trigger failure | DB error mid-trigger-transaction | status stays `viewed` (already committed); no rows; Sentry captures; 200 still returned to client | fail-open (Tier 2) |
+| Manual start (non-viewed) | POST start on a shortlisted app | rows created exactly as auto-trigger would; 200 | ownership/archived prechecks as status PATCH |
+| Manual start on declined | POST start, choice=declined | no rows; 200 (suppressed — the Off state hides manual actions, RC4.3) | N/A |
+| Skip a queued row | POST skip on `employer_ref` with a queued row | guarded `queued → skipped`, `next_attempt_at=NULL`; `reference_call_skipped` audit; 200 | N/A |
+| Skip before trigger | POST skip on `landlord_ref`, no live row | skipped row created with contact snapshot (reserves slot); audit; 200 | N/A |
+| Skip idempotent | POST skip on an already-skipped slot | no-op; 200 | N/A |
+| Skip a non-queued live row | POST skip on a `contact_initiated` row | 409 `Conflict` (skip is a queued/pre-trigger action) | branded 409 |
+| Re-enable | POST re-enable on a skipped slot | guarded `skipped → queued`, `next_attempt_at=now()`; `reference_call_re_enabled` audit; 200 | N/A |
+| Re-enable no skipped row | POST re-enable, no skipped row | 404 (nothing to re-enable) | branded 404 |
+| Unknown slot | POST skip with `:slot=fake` | 400 (invalid slot) | branded 400 |
+| Not owner / archived vacancy | POST start, landlord doesn't own app | 404 / 422 (same prechecks as status PATCH) | branded |
+
