+## Design Notes
+
+- **No migration (briefing was stale).** The briefing's "Migration: ALTER TYPE reference_call_status ADD VALUE 'skipped'" step is based on a pre-RC2.1 reading. RC2.1 already added `'skipped'` (A6) and `update_reference_call_status.sql` already clears `next_attempt_at` on `'skipped'` entry. `audit_log.event_type` is `TEXT`, so the 3 new event strings need no migration. Verified on disk before writing any code (field-notes rule: briefings can be stale).
+- **Why post-commit fail-open for the trigger (not in-transaction with the status UPDATE).** The hook sits at the `maybe_send_shortlist_notification` call site, which is post-commit by design (the status UPDATE + its audit commit, THEN the side-effects run). Making the reference-trigger in-transaction would require restructuring `apply_status_update` and would roll back a viewing-status change on a reference-row DB hiccup — wrong trade-off (the landlord should always be able to mark a viewing done). The trigger runs in its OWN `pog.transaction` (row-creation + audit atomic within it), and at the outer level is fail-open (Sentry on failure). The manual-start API is the human-recoverable fallback: if the trigger silently fails, the landlord can start checks explicitly. This matches the established posture at this exact call site.
+- **Why skip handles the no-live-row case (A6 "before trigger").** A6 says skipped is "treated as live for the slot unique index" and the landlord can exclude "at/before trigger". If skip only handled `queued → skipped`, a landlord could not pre-exclude a slot before the viewing — the auto-trigger would later create a `queued` row for it. Creating a `skipped` row directly (with the contact snapshot) reserves the slot, and the auto-trigger's `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` (the skipped row is live, so it conflicts) respects it. This makes skip idempotent and correct across the full A6 semantic at the API layer RC4.3's UI consumes.
+- **Why whole-application manual start (not per-slot).** FR-RC4 says "per slot or whole application". The whole-application start (call the core creation function) is the auto-trigger equivalent and the common case ("start checks for this applicant"). Per-slot granularity is achieved via skip (start all applicable, skip the ones you don't want) — a coherent UX that needs no second route. A `?slot=` variant can be added in RC4.3 if the UI demands it; RC2.3's AC is satisfied by the whole-application path.
+- **Why a dedicated `re_enable_reference_call.sql` (not reuse `update_reference_call_status`).** The existing guarded transition's `next_attempt_at` CASE only clears (terminal/skipped entry) or preserves (other transitions) — it never re-arms to `now()`. Re-enable MUST re-arm so the sweep (RC3.5) picks the row up. A dedicated query expresses that in one statement and keeps the re-arm intent explicit. Skip reuses `update_reference_call_status` because its clearing CASE is exactly right for `queued → skipped`.
+- **Why the slot-selection is landlord_ref XOR character_ref.** AD-13 + FR-RC3: the primary applicant's "landlord-ref slot (or character-ref when `never_rented_before`)". The application form swaps character in for landlord when the applicant never rented — they are the SAME slot (two flavours), never both. Employer is a separate, independent slot. So at most 2 rows per trigger. Co-applicant employer refs are schema-ready (`owner_label`) but auto-triggering them is deferred (AD-13 — contact volume doubles).
+- **ON CONFLICT + partial index + RETURNING.** Postgres infers the conflict against `idx_reference_call_live` when the `ON CONFLICT (cols) WHERE <predicate>` matches the index's predicate verbatim. `RETURNING id::text` yields 0 rows on conflict (no audit) / 1 row on insert (audit) — the exact signal for "audit only what was created". If Squirrel's parser rejects the `ON CONFLICT ... DO NOTHING ... RETURNING` shape, the fallback is a plain `INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` without RETURNING plus a follow-up read — but the RETURNING form is expected to codegen cleanly (Squirrel already handles the plain INSERT RETURNING in `insert_reference_call`).
+- **Test-DB port:** sibling worktrees hold 54321/54322/54323/54324; this story runs its own container on 54325 (`rt-rc2-3-test-db`) for Squirrel codegen + integration, torn down afterwards.
+- **`reference_checks` module is RC2.3's deliverable.** `trigger.gleam` owns creation + the 3 API handlers for RC2.3. RC4.3 may add `actions_handler.gleam` for the richer UI-driven actions (take over, correct, substitute); RC2.3 does not pre-empt that.
